From b8f45cffd71d7af35ff1c6af494cc31a7ce682d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kycube <kf1178@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:26:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] xteink-x4pro: RTC IO stored-value overlay replaces the
 rtcio access logger

The RTC-domain pad configuration both firmwares program around deep sleep (TOUCH_PAD3/5/6/7/13/14,
XTAL_32P/N, PAD_DAC2: hold, pull, sleep isolation) reads back as written; the W1TS/W1TC pairs
act on OUT/ENABLE/STATUS. No electrical behaviour, no overlap with the RTC_CNTL sleep overlay.
state.rtcio = {reads, writes, pad_writes, hold_mask}; no x4pro/rtcio logger lines remain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/misc/meson.build           |   1 +
 hw/misc/x4pro_rtcio.c         | 141 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/xtensa/xteink_x4pro.c      |  20 ++++-
 include/hw/misc/x4pro_rtcio.h |  26 +++++++
 4 files changed, 186 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/x4pro_rtcio.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/misc/x4pro_rtcio.h

